From 69fa19f66f0fac0ca394e2b5e44a963e6ba80293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:41:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] rtems-esp-wifi: add ESP32-C5 target support

Consolidated from the following downstream patches. Original rationale
and provenance are retained below; source licensing is unchanged.

Original-patch: 0002-rtems-esp-wifi-add-esp32c5-support.patch
Original-author: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-15T16:41:19+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: 2ba930284aabe2240ddc9f37b8801509e0b6f4e5

rtems-esp-wifi: add ESP32-C5 target and register layouts

Select the C5 PHY configuration, eFuse base and modem clock/reset registers.
Configure direct-boot memory access and keep the RFPLL shim confined to C6.
Match ESP-IDF coexistence-disabled callbacks instead of reporting failures.

Original-patch: 0006-esp32c5-preserve-pma-and-detect-xtal.patch
Original-author: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-19T12:50:26+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: c83b8dbcbf3925c090f8e88299ac5fcdcf1e4480

rtems-esp-wifi: preserve C5 memory attributes and detect XTAL

Keep the ROM/BSP PMA entries when bringing up the modem. Clearing them can
stall execution on physical C5 boards. Read PCR_CLK_XTAL_FREQ for the PHY
so that C5 boards with either a 40 MHz or 48 MHz crystal use the right value.
